# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Load before starting Claude Code:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a; claude
#
# ASTA_API_KEY — Ai2 Asta Scientific Corpus Tool, used by the cross-field
# methodology search. Request one (free) at:
#   https://share.hsforms.com/1L4hUh20oT3mu8iXJQMV77w3ioxm
#
# Optional. Without it the arXiv and PubMed legs run normally and the
# cross-field pass is skipped with a notice. Do NOT run that pass unauthenticated:
# Asta's search tools do not return a clean auth error, they hang ~271s and then
# fail with a misleading ConnectionRefusedError.
ASTA_API_KEY=
#
# SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY — optional, speed only. scripts/link_papers.py fetches
# every paper's references and SPECTER2 embedding in one Semantic Scholar batch
# request, and scripts/fetch_fulltext.py looks up each paper's ids and
# open-access PDF there. Without a key both share a public quota that rejects
# most requests at busy times; the linker retries for up to 10 minutes and then
# skips linking, and the fetcher skips that source for the paper.
# Free key: https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api#api-key-form
SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=
#
# UNPAYWALL_EMAIL — optional. Unpaywall's API takes no key, only a contact
# email. With it set, scripts/fetch_fulltext.py uses Unpaywall as its last
# open-access source, and the paper-search MCP server enables its own Unpaywall
# lookup (.mcp.json passes it through). Without it that source is skipped and
# the fetcher says so in its report; the other sources are unaffected.
UNPAYWALL_EMAIL=
#
# OPENALEX_API_KEY — optional. scripts/find_papers.py chases citations through
# OpenAlex, which needs no key: without one the daily budget is $0.10, about
# 1,000 filter requests, and a chase round takes around ten (a seed found only
# by title costs ten more). A free key raises the budget to $1 a day, for large
# vaults or several runs a day. Make an account at openalex.org and copy the
# key from https://openalex.org/settings/api
OPENALEX_API_KEY=
